<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two South Korean firms buy 21,500T U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two South Korean firms buy 21,500T U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd and Cheiljedang Corp on Friday bought a total of 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat from Japanese trading firm Marubeni Corp, traders in Seoul said.</p>
<p>Cheiljedang bought 9,000 tonnes at basis over March futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Shipment was set for January 1-31 from the Pacific Northwest to the southeastern ports of Pusan and Ulsan, they said.</p>
<p>Officials at the two companies confirmed the deals but declined to give details.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follows:</p>
<p>DONGAH FLOUR MILLS CO LTD</p>
<p>  TYPE OF WHEAT	   TONNE   PRICE/TONNE(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		4,800   $178.94</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8 pct)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  300   $182.62</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 pct)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,700   $186.29</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,700   $191.07</p>
